 "script": {
  "hook": "A user taps your link and lands on the home screen, not the product.",
  "question": "Design deep links for a mobile app.",
  "trap": "The trap: a custom URL scheme. Any app can claim it, and if your app is missing, the link just dies.",
  "steps": [
   "Use verified links. Universal links on iOS and app links on Android, backed by a file on your own domain.",
   "Route in one place. Parse the url into a typed destination, check login, then navigate.",
   "Handle not installed. Send them to the store, then a deferred deep link restores the destination after first open.",
   "Always fall back. Unknown or old links open the web page or home, never a blank error."
  ],
  "takeaway": "Own the domain, route in one place, and always have a fallback.",
  "teaser": "Tomorrow: push notifications.",
  "cta": "Comment M S D for the free cheatsheet."
 },
